/-!
# Harmonic polylogarithms at `1`: words with trailing zeros, weights four and five

The values `H(w; 1)` of the words `w` over `{0, 1, -1}` of weight four and five whose first
letter is not `1` and whose last letter is `0` (and which are not all zeros): the 14 such words
of weight four not already in `QED.Polylog.HPLValues4`, and all 53 of weight five.

For `w = u 0ᵏ` (`u` ending in a nonzero letter), the shuffle product
`H(0; 1) H(u 0ᵏ⁻¹; 1) = ∑_{x ∈ 0 ш u 0ᵏ⁻¹} H(x; 1)` has left side `0` (`H(0; 1) = log 1`), and
contains `H(w; 1)` with multiplicity `k`; every other word has `k - 1` trailing zeros. This
determines `H(w; 1)` recursively from the convergent values of `QED.Polylog.HPLValuesAlt4`,
`QED.Polylog.HPLValuesAlt5A`–`QED.Polylog.HPLValuesAlt5D` (the statements were generated by a
script; the proofs are checked by Lean).
-/

@[expose] public section

open Real

namespace QED.Polylog.HPL

open Letter

theorem hpl_zero_zero_negOne_zero_at_one :
    hpl [zero, zero, negOne, zero] 1 =
      -7 / 240 * π ^ 4 := by
  have h := hpl_one_mul_hpl_one (u := [zero]) (v := [zero, zero, negOne])
    (by decide) (by decide)
  simp [shuffle_cons_cons, hpl_zero_at_one] at h
  linear_combination (-1) * h + (-3) * hpl_zero_zero_zero_negOne_at_one

